# fixedbugs, defect 2364, lane p239-land-a, 2026-11-09, the shape beside
# defect 2357's stand-in case.
#
# This program's own group names `packs-four.h`, which leaves `#pragma
# pack(4)` set, and it holds the fetched package `pt`'s record, so its unit
# reads the package's `pt.h` after it and lays `pt_point` out at a multiple of
# 4, where the package's own unit lays it out at a multiple of 8. No file
# stands in for `pt.h`: the package's header is read, and the program's own
# header changes it. A unit's own headers come first, so no order makes the
# two alike, and the program is refused, told where it spells the record.
use <pt>/pt

extern "packs-four.h"
    function four() -> i32

function main()
    p: pt.Point = pt.make(x: 3, y: 4)  #~ ffi_record_two_layouts
    print(p.x + p.y + to_i64(four()).must())
